From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [model] feat: Qwen3.5's monkey patch on transformers 5.16 and
 later

From transformers 5.16 a Qwen3.5 decoder layer holds its type as block_type instead of layer_type, and the
GatedDeltaNet no longer holds its kernels as attributes: causal_conv1d_fn, causal_conv1d_update,
torch_chunk_gated_delta_rule and torch_recurrent_gated_delta_rule are functions of the modeling module, which run
causal-conv1d's or FLA's kernel when that package is installed (modeling_qwen3_5.py: the attributes at 5.12.1:420-423
and layer_type at :760; the functions at 5.16.1:199-331 and 5.22.0:235-424, block_type at 5.16.1:747 and
5.22.0:852; the MoE model alike). verl's decoder and GatedDeltaNet forwards read layer_type and the attributes, so on
5.16 and later the first forward raised AttributeError.

The decoder forward now reads block_type when the layer has it and layer_type otherwise, and the GatedDeltaNet
forward takes each kernel from the layer when the layer has it and from the layer's module otherwise. The
convolution gets its tensors positionally: the torch fallback behind the module function names its input
hidden_states where causal-conv1d names it x, and the wrapper drops the keywords its implementation does not take
(integrations/hub_kernels.py:860 in 5.16.1). _packed_chunk_gated_delta_rule takes the chunk function instead of the
layer. On transformers 5.12 nothing changes. This is upstream's change to this file in #8390 (f78fd05).

On 5.16 and later the module's causal_conv1d_fn is never None, so packed rows still reach transformers' convolution,
which cannot keep packed sequences apart without the causal-conv1d package; the next patch sends them to FLA's
kernel again.
